  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 224 AM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nUpper-level ridging will build across the desert southwest through \nthe upcoming weekend and into the middle of next week. A dry \nnorthwest flow aloft will become established across our area on the \nnortheast periphery of the high. \n\nCanadian surface high pressure shifts east of the area Saturday, \nwith gusty south winds developing ahead of a weak approaching \nshortwave and associated cold front. Appears the cold front will \nenter northwest Nebraska mid-morning Saturday, and then track \nsouthward through all of the area by early Saturday evening. \nTemperatures have trended up Saturday as deep mixing brings warmer \nair aloft to the surface. Highs in the mid to upper 70s are now \nexpected across a large part of the area. Weak cold air advection, \nand another high pressure center from Canada, will slide \nsoutheastward behind the front Saturday night. This will cool highs \nback into the mid and upper 60s Sunday. \n\nThe surface high slides east of the region Monday. The surface \npressure gradient will tighten between the high to the east and a \ndeepening leeward trough to the west. This will result in gusty \nsouth through the day Monday. Gusts in excess of 40 mph look likely \nacross the Sandhills and portions of north central Nebraska. Winds \ndecrease for Tuesday as the leeward trough shifts eastward across \nthe area. A warm up is slated for next week, with highs Monday in \nthe mid 60s to mid 70s, mid 70s to near 80 Tuesday and 70s for \nWednesday.",
